      "summary": "Man’s gown (boubou, tobe) made from four sheets of European cotton sheeting, dyed indigo in Africa and sewn together to form a rectangular gown with square sleeves. At the front is sewn an irregularly shaped pocket of the same material. Both the front and the back are extensively embroidered with hand-sewn decoration in white, green, peach, red, light blue, dark blue and yellow European cotton thread, in patterns that include knives, stars and spirals. The decoration on the front is asymmetrical; that on the back is symmetrical. The sleeves and base are hemmed by machine.",
